{"type":"text","timestamp":1778527416748,"sessionID":"ses_1e78fd73fffeBJ9rBjHTOVNbnC","part":{"id":"prt_e187d076c0012txGzRq13yLbC4","messageID":"msg_e187cebe9001tWN7an2aiyb9KY","sessionID":"ses_1e78fd73fffeBJ9rBjHTOVNbnC","type":"text","text":"---\n**Plan:**\n1. Create a new term `podocytopathy` with the provided definition and references.\n2. Set the parent term to `MONDO:0019722` (glomerular disorder).\n3. Set `MONDO:0006835` (minimal change disease) and `MONDO:0100313` (focal segmental glomerulosclerosis) as children of `podocytopathy`.\n4. Assign the creator ORCID: `https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0876-0331`.\n5. Use a new MONDO ID (e.g., `MONDO:7770018`).\n6. Update the `is_a` relationships of the children terms to point to `podocytopathy`.\n7. Validate and normalize the ontology.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. **Create new term `podocytopathy`**:\n   - ID: `MONDO:7770018`\n   - Name: `podocytopathy`\n   - Def: \"A group of glomerular diseases caused by the structural or functional impairment of podocytes which drive proteinuria or nephrotic syndrome.\" [PMID:32792490, PMID:25684864, PMID:38804512]\n   - Parent: `MONDO:0019722` (glomerular disorder)\n   - Creator: `https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0876-0331`\n   - Issue: `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10149`\n2. **Update children**:\n   - `MONDO:0006835` (minimal change disease): `is_a` → `MONDO:7770018`\n   - `MONDO:0100313` (focal segmental glomerulosclerosis): `is_a` → `MONDO:7770018`\n3. **Validation**:\n   - Run `robot convert` to check syntax.\n   - Run `make NORM`.\n---\n\nLet's start.\n\nFirst, I'll create the new term. Since the requested ID range for new terms is `MONDO:777xxxx`, and the last one was `MONDO:7770017`, I'll use `MONDO:7770018`.\n\nI'll create the new term in `terms/podocytopathy.obo` first.\n\nWait, I should check if `MONDO:0019722` exists.\n","time":{"start":1778527307628,"end":1778527416747}}}
